<article class="env-lemma" id="0D0P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D0P">Lemma <span data-tag="0D0P">71.18.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ B$-module. Let $Z_ k \subset S$ be the closed subscheme cut out by $\text{Fit}_ k(\mathcal{F})$, see Section <a href="/tag/0CZ3" data-tag="0CZ3">71.5</a>. Let $B' \to B$ be the blowup of $B$ in $Z_ k$ and let $\mathcal{F}'$ be the strict transform of $\mathcal{F}$. Then $\mathcal{F}'$ can locally be generated by $\leq k$ sections. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Follows from the case of schemes (Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CZP" data-tag="0CZP">31.36.1</a>) by étale localization (Lemma <a href="/tag/0863" data-tag="0863">71.18.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>